{"name":"California Dreamin’","hex":"#93807f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"California Dreamin'","blocks":[{"text":"\"California Dreamin'\" is a song written by John and Michelle Phillips. The best-known version is by the Mamas & the Papas, who released it as a single in December 1965."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/%22California_Dreamin%27%22_picture_sleeve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Dreamin'","wikidata":"Q1026811"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California","wikidata":"Q99"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/California_Dreamin%27_Beach_Boys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/California_Dreamin%27_Beach_Boys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalifornia_Dreamin'_Beach_Boys.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500